Speaker 1: But it goes out of its way to give you the context that matters for the story, and then everything else either doesn't matter or you're going to learn it in the course of reading these issues.

586
00:43:28,691 --> 00:43:31,060
Speaker 1: This has been Geek Nights with Rim and Scott.

587
00:43:31,120 --> 00:43:33,630
Speaker 1: Special thanks to DJ Pretzel for the opening theme.

588
00:43:33,830 --> 00:43:39,850
Speaker 0: Be sure to visit our website at FrontRowClue.com for show notes, discussion, links, and more.

589
00:43:40,332 --> 00:43:43,022
Speaker 1: Remember, Geek Nights is not one but four different shows.

590
00:43:43,324 --> 00:43:44,890
Speaker 1: Mondays are science and technology.

591
00:43:45,030 --> 00:43:46,775
Speaker 1: Tuesdays, gaming and games.

592
00:43:46,876 --> 00:43:48,701
Speaker 1: Wednesdays are animation and comics.

593
00:43:49,022 --> 00:43:51,510
Speaker 1: Thursdays are arbitrary and indiscriminate.

594
00:43:52,230 --> 00:43:57,090
Speaker 1: Geek Nights is distributed under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 international license.

595
00:43:57,610 --> 00:44:01,880
Speaker 0: Geek Nights is recorded live with no studio and no audience.

596
00:44:02,362 --> 00:44:05,830
Speaker 0: But unlike those other late shows, it's actually recorded at night.

597
00:44:06,271 --> 00:44:19,110
Speaker 1: And the Patreon patrons for this episode of Geek Nights are Ella Joyce, Linky G, Jirrei Lillie, Tenebrae, Chris, The Dog, Christopher, Clinton Walton, Finn, Joel Hayes, Penny Rymer, Rebecca Dunst, Sam Erickson, Shervin Von Hurl, and several people whose names I will not say.

598
00:44:19,650 --> 00:44:23,830
Speaker 1: I'm going to cut this short because I'm going to go try to watch the PWHL game in the other room.

599
00:44:24,010 --> 00:44:29,710
Speaker 1: So tonight, I leave you with... Let me tell you something about human's nephew.

600
00:44:32,336 --> 00:44:34,260
Speaker 1: There are wonderful, friendly people.

601
00:44:35,220 --> 00:44:42,645
Speaker 1: As long as their bellies are full and their holosuites will deprive them of full sonic showers.

602
00:44:52,451 --> 00:45:08,750
Speaker 1: With their lives in jeopardy over an extended period of time, and those same friendly, intelligent, wonderful people will become as nasty and as violent as the most bloodthirsty Klingon.

603
00:45:11,177 --> 00:45:11,869
Speaker 0: You don't believe me?

604
00:45:14,870 --> 00:45:15,932
Speaker 0: Look at those faces.

605
00:45:17,393 --> 00:45:18,234
Speaker 1: Look in their eyes.

606
00:45:21,919 --> 00:45:22,900
Speaker 1: You know I'm right, don't you?

